00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:10,880
Is it Spectre?

351
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:12,080
It's Spectre.

352
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:12,960
Spectre, okay.

353
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:18,160
I use Spectre a lot too because that gives me, you know, a different thing.

354
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:27,120
And usually I'll sit there in front of the same flower or waterfall or whatever for like five minutes switching between apps and trying different exposures and all sorts of different things.

355
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:36,720
And it feels like what it felt like when I first got, even maybe before my SLR, when I first got like a digital camera that had manual modes that I could.

356
00:30:37,280 --> 00:30:41,520
play with and it sort of unlock this sloppy creative freedom.

