00:48:00,160 --> 00:48:03,040
I you've talked about it a lot in lots of different ways.

542
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:18,080
I'll link to blog posts, but I'd love to just get some sort of the highlights for why you decided to do that and then how you approached doing that without or at least with lowering the amount of angry mob that was sent your way as possible.

543
00:48:18,960 --> 00:48:21,840
So we're careful to point out we're not a subscription app.

544
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:24,800
We offer a pay once option or a subscription.

545
00:48:25,360 --> 00:48:26,240
And that's the first trick.

546
00:48:26,480 --> 00:48:27,040
Ooh, okay.

547
00:48:27,280 --> 00:48:27,840
Good call out.

548
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:30,240
That's a really important thing.

549
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:30,880
Yeah.

550
00:48:31,840 --> 00:48:41,520
So yeah, I'd say that a lot of the V or with the Mk 2, I lost track of how many hours we spent figuring out the right way to navigate this.

551
00:48:42,960 --> 00:48:48,160
Even up to a month before launch, just figuring out what exactly we're doing, what we're giving away.

552
00:48:49,120 --> 00:48:53,920
Originally, we were talking about having a separate app and then converting users over and giving them upgrade price.

553
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:55,760
That's really complicated.

554
00:48:57,280 --> 00:49:11,520
I don't know if it was you Sebastian, it was just like, why don't we just give all of our V one users a free upgrade to Mark two and a year of upgrades for free, and then we'll figure it out like a year later how we're going to transition people over to new features.

555
00:49:12,160 --> 00:49:14,960
So, um, but yeah, it was just like a it was a lot of thinking.

556
00:49:15,680 --> 00:49:15,760
Yeah.

557
00:49:16,240 --> 00:49:21,040
And Rebecca was also coming in at this time and that was absolutely invaluable as an extra perspective.

558
00:49:21,200 --> 00:49:24,080
You just wanted to, to, to really have an open mind about it.

559
00:49:24,480 --> 00:49:27,520
And there's a lot of ways to do this wrong, you know?

560
00:49:27,680 --> 00:49:31,920
Um, and the reason we're moving towards this, I mean, it's, it's because we're greedy.

561
00:49:32,320 --> 00:49:34,240
We're greedy developers and we want all the money.

562
00:49:34,560 --> 00:49:41,440
Um, it's, it's, people seem to think, but no, it's we, we had been giving, um, how it's turning five next year.

563
00:49:41,600 --> 00:49:45,840
We've been giving, uh, putting out really substantial updates for years and years and years.

564
00:49:46,160 --> 00:50:02,320
And, um, we realized that we're in the difficult position position where we're going to have to make the choice that if we wanted to run this as a business and if we really wanted to just work on this full time, which we did, because we loved working on it, it's a dream to our users, like, thank you for letting me wake up and do this every day, it's awesome.

